    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26339" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lēto</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lētho</span></b> ), āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to kill, slay</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lycurgiden letavit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
					505</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paris hunc letat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg. Cul. 323</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">letata corpora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					3, 55</span></i>
			 (the conjectural reading letatus, <i><span class="en">Cic. Leg.
				3, 8, 19</span></i>, is very dub.; v. Orell. ad loc., where leto
			datus is proposed; B. and K., necatus).</div>
